    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two files are the base and the audit-capture helper). The full suite is green.\n\nDone. On a successful owner create, `RespondWithOwnerCreated` now emits an audit line via the `AUDIT` logger:\n\n```\nINFO AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-11\n```\n\nThe change (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`):\n- Added a `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` logger.\n- Log the owner id, customerCode, and registrationDate in the responder \u2014 the last step of the create pipeline, so it fires only after `SaveOwner` succeeds and the owner has its id assigned.\n\n`registrationDate` logs as the `LocalDate` ISO string (`2026-08-11`), matching the JSON serialization the test asserts against. `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1).",
